Consider the state equation $$\mathop X\limits^ \bullet  \left( t \right) = Ax\left( t \right)$$ 
<br>Given : $${e^{AT}} = \left[ {\matrix{
   {{e^{ - t}} + t{e^{ - t}}} &amp; {t{e^{ - t}}}  \cr 
   { - t{e^{ - t}}} &amp; {{e^{ - t}} - t{e^{ - t}}}  \cr 

 } } \right]$$ 
<p>(a) Find a set of states $${x_1}\left( 1 \right)$$ and $${x_2}\left( 1 \right)$$ such that $${x_1}\left( 2 \right) = 2.$$
<br>(b) Show  that $$\,{\left( {s{\rm I} - A} \right)^{ - t}} = \Phi \left( s \right) = {1 \over \Delta }\left[ {\matrix{
   {s + 2} &amp; 1  \cr 
   { - 1} &amp; s  \cr 

 } } \right];$$  $$\Delta  = {\left( {s + 1} \right)^2}$$ 
<br>(c) From $$\Phi \left( s \right),$$ find the matrix $$A$$.</p>

